 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
 *   **Rotation Illusion:** Without simulated attenuation ($\alpha=0$), viewing in a rotating format (cine display) may cause an illusion of reversal of rotation [S1, unofficial]. Adding attenuation prevents this [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Contrast Degradation:** Simulated attenuation and noise cause contrast degradation compared to slice data. For a cylindrical phantom, contrast degradation is 19% for Max0.0, 32% for Max0.024, and 54% for Max0.049 [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Loss of Low-Uptake Regions:** Areas of decreased uptake are not shown. In objects with mildly increased uptake centrally and more intense peripheral uptake (e.g., tumor with necrotic center), the central activity will not be visible [S1, unofficial].
